const QUESTIONS = [["UI-OPEN-01","Kiosk","Confirm shared-account provisioning for each kiosk station, badge encoding and provisioning, and the behavior when a punch cannot be confirmed. Badge-only authentication and 60-second timeouts are approved (§5.5).","Needed for the kiosk journeys in Germany and Poland.","High","PU-09, KI-01, KI-02"],["UI-OPEN-02","Kiosk","Confirm the attached-scanner badge input: encoding, scan timing, and invalid-scan handling. The kiosk requests no job or project barcode (§3.1, §5.5).","Decides the badge-scan input.","High","PU-09, PU-10"],["UI-OPEN-03","Platform","Confirm the browser, device, operating-system, kiosk hardware, viewport, resolution and responsive-breakpoint support matrix.","Sets the responsive targets.","High","—"],["UI-OPEN-04","Time Off","Confirm eligible request types, how the three-day period is counted, notification channels, and exception handling when an employee has no assigned Manager. The initial rule approves an eligible request still Submitted after three days without a Manager decision.","Eligibility details and no-Manager routing remain open; the three-day Approved outcome is documented.","High","TO-05, TO-06"],["UI-OPEN-05","Labor category","Confirm the Administrator-managed labor-category profiles: which apply to whom, how many levels, level labels and order, and how values are prefilled or chosen manually.","Drives project and category fields on every entry screen.","High","CC-04"],["UI-OPEN-06","Approval","Confirm hourly project-time approval roles, routing, review steps and statuses. Salaried project hours do not require approval.","Defines the review queue and statuses.","High","GR-08, GR-10"],["UI-OPEN-07","Weekly calendar","Confirm saved-entry editing and current or prior-period permissions (§9), required project and category fields, and how a completed week is reviewed. The week runs Monday to Sunday, and Save marks salaried hours Recorded (§5.2).","Defines the salaried calendar.","High","GR-01, GR-09"],["UI-OPEN-08","Time Off","Confirm eligible Time Off request types and duration options, the Sick Time lookback limit, and how to handle an unavailable current balance. Actual request statuses are Approved, Refused, Submitted, and Cancelled.","Defines the policy matrix and balance fallback; employee-facing status mapping is documented.","High","TO-01, TO-02, TO-03, TO-04, TO-05, TO-06, TO-07"],["UI-OPEN-09","Dashboard","Define the project dashboard in a future discussion (audience, measures, layout, thresholds, data freshness). No design is approved yet, so it is not in this demo.","Scope not elicited.","Medium","—"],["UI-OPEN-10","Punch transfers","Define the pre-punch transfer lifecycle: persistence and expiry, cancellation or replacement, navigation and sign-in behavior, and effects of project changes or a failed Punch In.","The prototype shows pending categories but does not establish production persistence.","High","PU-01, PU-04"],["UI-OPEN-11","Odoo","Confirm the Odoo project catalog source and access, assignment rules and permissions, active-project filtering, saved visibility and assignments, refresh, and outage handling.","Demo catalog and added assignments are local simulations.","High","PU-01, PU-05, PU-12"],["UI-OPEN-12","Employee type","Identify the UKG hourly or salaried field and define handling of missing or unclear values.","Decides whether an employee uses Punch or Project hours.","High","PU-11"],["UI-OPEN-13","Access","Define Employee defaults, Manager and Administrator assignment, additional-role handling, and shared-kiosk configuration.","Default Employee access remains a working assumption.","High","TO-05"],["Q-01","Timecard","What is the pay period per country (weekly, bi-weekly, semi-monthly, monthly)?","Defines the period dates, navigation boundaries and period totals.","High","TC-01, TC-02"],["Q-02","Populations","Which populations must punch, which may use the project hours calendar, and which use both?","Drives the landing view.","High","PU-11"],["Q-03","Exceptions","Which punch conditions should appear as inline cell indicators (missed out, late in, early out or short break), and with what grace minutes? The current view has no separate Exceptions list or absence label.","Controls which timecard cells receive attention cues.","High","TC-03"],["Q-04","Breaks","What are the break rules per country (paid or unpaid, minimum length, automatic deduction)?","Changes break punches and totals.","High","PU-03"],["Q-05","Edit rights","Will hourly employees be allowed to change recorded In/Out punches? If yes, confirm eligible groups, editable periods, required reasons, approval handling and direct-save versus Manager-review behavior. Editing is currently disabled and hidden; no correction-request route is assumed.","Determines whether a future employee punch-edit journey is enabled. Current My Timecard remains read-only.","Medium","TC-04"],["Q-06","Projects","Is a project required for every punch, or can a punch start without one?","Affects punch-in speed.","High","PU-01, PU-05"],["Q-07","Approval","Do employees approve their own timecards at period end? (Out of scope in the current draft.)","Would add employee approval back.","Medium","removed from scope"],["Q-08","Totals","The current view shows Project and Task / LOB totals only. Should UKG pay-code, overtime or premium totals be added in a later iteration?","Keeps the project/task-only Totals view explicit and identifies possible future additions.","Medium","TC-07"],["Q-09","Rejection","Is a note mandatory when rejecting project time? (It is required for Time Off.)","Changes the rejection dialog.","Medium","GR-10"],["Q-10","Scanner","Which devices and scanners will the German and Polish warehouses use (shared tablet, handheld scanner, web)?","Affects kiosk layout and scan input.","High","PU-09, PU-10"],["Q-12","Integration","Is project allocation carried by UKG Activities or by punch transfers?","Determines the write shape for PU-04.","High","PU-04"],["Q-13","Weekly calendar","Which teams get Copy and Archive instead of auto-population, and what is the project-count threshold?","Decides GR-06 and GR-07 scope.","Medium","GR-02, GR-06, GR-07"],["Q-14","Reminders","When and how often should time-entry reminders go out per region?","Configures GR-11.","Low","GR-11"]];